{"number": 33, "text": "                    Exercises\n\n\n            13.1    Look  at the picture and answer the\n                    questions.\n                       What does the woman  need to tidy up?\n                       What does she need to sweep up?\n                    3  What must she hang up?                        er\n                       What are jumbled up on the floor?\n                       How  might she feel when she has\n                       cleared everything up?\n\n            13.2    Choose  the best verb from B to fill the gaps in this email. Use a different verb in each gap and\n                    write it in the correct form.\n\n                                                                                   Reply          Forward\n                Hi, Gina!\n                How  are things with you? Hope all's well. Has your cousin             (1) up yet? We\n                certainly need him around to               (2) this place up a bit! Besides which, | need\n                his help in the garden. An old tree blew down last week and | need to            (3) up\n                the branches. When  he eventually                (4) up, let's try out that new club that’s\n                                (5) up in Market Street.\n                Love, Esme\n\n\n             13.3    Choose the correct word to complete these sentences. Sometimes there is more than one\n                     possible answer.\n                     1 Sam                 up too much time on the first exam question and didn’t finish the paper.\n                       a) clogged     b) used    c) divided   d) showed\n                     2 Guess who                 up at midnight last night!\n                       a) showed      b) livened   c) hung    d) turned\n                     3 Please could you               up these onions for me?\n                       a) divide    b) turn    c) chop    d) clog\n                     4 Sofia spent ages     